.TH VAULT-MV 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-mv \- rename or move a stored file or folder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault mv
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.I OLD NEW
.br
.B vault rename
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames \fIOLD\fR, a file or a folder and everything under it, to
\fINEW\fR. If \fINEW\fR ends in / or names an existing folder, \fIOLD\fR
moves into it, keeping its base name, as with
.BR mv (1).
Fails, changing nothing, if any new name exists or is not a valid vault
path. File contents are not re-encrypted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-cp (1),
.BR vault\-rm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
